---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Siddharth Sahoo"
  description="About Siddharth Sahoo: developer, visual creator and builder of software, automations and internet things."
  pageClass="about-page"
>
  <header class="page-hero page-hero-v2" data-scroll-progress="viewport">
    <span class="kicker">03 / About</span>
    <h1>One person. Two toolkits.</h1>
    <div class="page-hero-copy">
      <div class="micro">SID / FLAC / 11SID11</div>
      <p>I am Siddharth Sahoo. I build software, edit video, design visual work and usually end up turning recurring annoyances into small products.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="shell about-shell">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <article class="about-block" data-scroll-progress="viewport">
        <span class="kicker">Developer</span>
        <h2>I like products with boundaries.</h2>
        <p>Local-first software, automation, browser tooling, PWAs and systems where the architecture explains what the product refuses to do as clearly as what it does.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-block" data-scroll-progress="viewport">
        <span class="kicker">Creative</span>
        <h2>I edit around attention.</h2>
        <p>Gaming and YouTube work taught me to notice where energy dies. That same instinct carries into thumbnails, brand content and visual systems: <strong>make the point readable, then get out of its way.</strong></p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-block" data-scroll-progress="viewport">
        <span class="kicker">Workflow</span>
        <h2>How I use AI.</h2>
        <p>I use Claude and Codex for research, implementation, and review. Git, tests, and manual QA decide what ships.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-block" data-scroll-progress="viewport">
        <span class="kicker">Away from the screen</span>
        <h2>Games, cameras, music, food, places.</h2>
        <p>Photography is usually the excuse to notice light. Gaming is partly recreation and partly an endless study in interface, pacing and feedback. I also sing, play guitar, cook, and travel when the calendar cooperates.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-interlude" data-scroll-progress="section" aria-label="Code and visual work">
    <div class="about-interlude-stage">
      <span class="about-interlude-word code">CODE</span>
      <p>Software and visual work use different tools. Both begin with a clear problem and end with something easier to use or understand.</p>
      <span class="about-interlude-word frame">FRAME</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-band about-contact" aria-label="Social profiles">
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">Talk</span>
      <h2>Where to find me.</h2>
      <p>X and Discord are the most direct ways to reach me. GitHub is where the code is. Instagram is where the visual side leaks out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-social-panel">
      <span class="kicker">Elsewhere</span>
      <nav class="social-directory" aria-label="Social links">
        <a class="social-directory-card" href="https://x.com/sid_flac" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          <span class="social-directory-index">01 / X</span><strong>@sid_flac</strong><span>Updates + quick conversations</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i>
        </a>
        <a class="social-directory-card" href="https://discord.com/users/456027988417314816" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          <span class="social-directory-index">02 / Discord</span><strong>Open profile</strong><span>Direct conversations</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i>
        </a>
        <a class="social-directory-card" href="https://github.com/11sid11" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          <span class="social-directory-index">03 / GitHub</span><strong>11sid11</strong><span>Code + public projects</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i>
        </a>
        <a class="social-directory-card" href="https://www.instagram.com/sid.flac/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          <span class="social-directory-index">04 / Instagram</span><strong>@sid.flac</strong><span>Visual work + experiments</span><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
